# console-serial.list -- the serial console redirect at major 8.
#
# /drv/notty forwards the console to the first `al' serial line.  vidsel falls
# back to this when no video board answers its probe, so EVERY dist must include
# it (directly or via the userland's console-both.list): without it a machine
# with no display has no console at all.
# PACKAGE.  The console drivers are the one part of a dist chosen by which
# MACHINE it is for, not by what an owner wants on it, so the role is
# `variant': a channel does not offer these three as a choice.  They are cut
# here because this repository links them: it knows which kernel they are bound
# to (build/drv/.drvstamp), which sources they are compiled from
# (build/.ulsrcmap) and which Lexicon articles describe them (man/).
package  console-serial
role     variant
# KINDS -- see commodore-900-dist's os/dist/PACKAGE-FORMAT.  `bin' is the
# list below; `src' is the complete corresponding source for every executable it
# installs and `man' the pages for those programs.  Both refuse to be cut from a
# guess.
kinds    src man
# A driver is documented under the device it provides, not under its file name:
# console(1) is the console /drv/notty redirects.
articles notty console

f	/drv/notty	755 0 1
